# ==============================================================================
# HealthHub Monorepo Environment Configuration Guide
# ==============================================================================
# HealthHub is composed of three applications. Each application manages its own
# isolated `.env` file within its respective subfolder:
#
# 1. Backend API (apps/api/.env)
#    - Node.js, Express, PostgreSQL, Prisma, JWT, Clerk, Razorpay, Google OAuth
#    - Copy from: apps/api/.env.example
#    - Run: cd apps/api && cp .env.example .env
#
# 2. Web Portal (apps/web/.env.local)
#    - Next.js (App Router), Tailwind CSS, Clerk, Razorpay Checkout
#    - Copy from: apps/web/.env.example
#    - Run: cd apps/web && cp .env.example .env.local
#    - Note: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_MODE=demo runs with typed synthetic fixtures (zero backend needed)
#            NEXT_PUBLIC_API_MODE=live connects to the Express API (http://localhost:4000)
#
# 3. Mobile App (apps/mobile/.env)
#    - React Native, Expo SDK 57, Clerk
#    - Copy from: apps/mobile/.env.example
#    - Run: cd apps/mobile && cp .env.example .env
#    - Note: EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_MODE=demo runs in-memory synthetic demo mode (zero backend needed)
#            EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_MODE=live connects to EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL
# ==============================================================================
